  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6d918094-5be2-5c2b-8a87-32149bc68429" activityNameId="052ad565-1534-5b9f-9ff8-5d05fe076700" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">3kWp facade installation, single-Si, laminated, integrated, at building</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: 3kWp facade installation, single-Si, laminated, integrated, at building
Photovoltaic installation with a capacity of 3kWp and a life time of 30 years installed in Asia and Pacific. The efficiency of single-Si PV modules is 17.9% (Fraunhofer ISE Photovoltaics Report 2019). The share of rejected or replaced PV modules is estimated at 3%. The inverter is assumed to be replaced once during the service life of the PV system.;
Synonyms: monocrystalline, single crystalline, silicon; 
UUID: 39186fa5-171d-4177-b2e2-d1deb283362d
All components for the installation of a 3kWp photovoltaic plant, energy use for the mounting, transport of materials and persons to the construction place. Disposal of components after end of life.
Location: Installation in Asia and Pacific.
Technology: Current technology for mounting of panels or laminates, electric installations and other components.
Time period: Average module efficiency in 2018.
Production volume: Total installed capacity in 2018: approximately 130 GWp in Asia and Pacific.
Sampling: Publication for efficiency, mounting systems and own estimations for other components. 
Extrapolations: Estimations for lifetime of PV modules (30a) and inverters (15a) as well as for transport distances. Modules are assumed to be produced in Asia and Pacific.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_39186fa5-171d-4177-b2e2-d1deb283362d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
